    "title": "Register for downtown tour of notable trees",
    "text": "A licensed arborist with Atlantic Lawn & Garden will lead a 90-minute tour of Champion Trees at 10 a.m. Saturday, July 25.\nThe free half-mile tour with David Frank will begin at St. Mark Church, 60 Narragansett Ave. He will answer questions about Champion Trees, which are noted by the Rhode Island Tree Council for their contributions to the economy, culture and ecology. Twelve of the 147 Champion Trees in Rhode Island are in Jamestown.\nThe tour is limited to 20 people. Register at jamestowntreecommittee@gmail.com.\nThe tour will be followed by a botanical printmaking workshop using gel plates at the Jamestown Arts Center, 18 Valley St. The cost is $25.",
    "summary": "A licensed arborist with Atlantic Lawn & Garden will lead a 90-minute tour of Champion Trees at 10 a.m. Saturday, July 25. The free half-mile tour with David Frank will begin at St. Mark Church, 60 Narragansett Ave. He will answer questions about Champion Trees, which are noted by the Rhode Island Tree Council for their contributions to the economy, culture and ecology. Twelve of the 147 Champion Trees in Rhode Island are in Jamestown. The tour will be followed by a botanical printmaking workshop using gel plates at the Jamestown Arts Center, 18 Valley St.",
